  "question": {
    "text": "Vipin and Shubham are playing a game with a coin, that comes up heads with a probability <math><mi>p</mi><mo>.</mo></math> They take turns flipping the coin until one of them wins, with Vipin going first. Vipin wins if he flips a heads and Shubham wins if he flips a tails. Given that the probability of Vipin winning the game is <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of <math><mi>p</mi></math> is <math><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mn>162</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The value of&nbsp;<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
